"""
panel_gen.glyphs -- the embedded Pilat outlines, kerning tables and house artwork.

What: pure data. LABEL_GLYPHS / LABEL_KERN are Pilat Bold (the jack, knob and title
labels), NAME_GLYPHS / NAME_KERN are Pilat Condensed Bold (the boxed module name),
WORDMARK_D is the VOXGLITCH wordmark and FRAME_D the module-name frame. Nothing here is
ever edited by hand; the tables are brief-panel-svg.md Appendix C and D and the artwork
is Appendix A and B, quoted verbatim so that a generator runs without the commercial
fonts, which must never be added to the repository.

Why a module of its own: the tables are two thirds of the original single-file
generator (scripts/generate_vx_drums_panels.py before 2026-09-16). Every generated panel
shares them unchanged, so they live once, here, and the layout code in panel_gen.text is
readable without scrolling past 200 lines of outlines.

Outline format: absolute SVG commands in font units with y DOWN (baseline 0, cap height
-700); transform="matrix(S/1000,0,0,S/1000,x,baseline)" places a glyph at S px.
KERN[a+b] is added to the advance of a when b follows.

Artwork format: the raw path data of the reference files (Illustrator 72 dpi units),
placed by panel_gen.elements.emit_branding with the RAW2PX matrix.
"""

